WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.767
A CTE is useful when one stage deserves a name.

00:00:03.767 --> 00:00:06.987
It can make a multi-step query easier to read.

00:00:06.987 --> 00:00:12.932
It is especially helpful when you need to calculate a window value first and filter that result later.

00:00:12.932 --> 00:00:16.782
Recursive queries also use the CTE structure.

00:00:16.782 --> 00:00:22.542
Use a CTE because it clarifies the logic, not simply because the query is long.

00:00:22.542 --> 00:00:28.922
A CTE gives a name to an intermediate result so a complex query can be read in stages.

00:00:28.922 --> 00:00:36.332
Use it to clarify grain changes and major transformations, not simply to break every two lines into a new

00:00:36.332 --> 00:00:42.550
block. A useful CTE name describes what the rows represent, such as patient_totals or ranked_visits.
